  "hindi": "हे लोगो, यह जान लो: महान् ब्रह्म (पवित्र वचन) बोलेगा। वह न पृथ्वी पर है और न द्युलोक में, जिसके द्वारा लता-पौधे जीती हैं।",
  "english": "Know this, O people: the great brahman (sacred utterance) will speak. That by which the plants live is neither on earth nor in heaven.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'idam ... vidatha' read as 'know this' (vidatha 2 pl. of √vid); vidatha could also be read as a noun (assembly), or idam as the object of vadiṣyati. 'tat ... yena' is read as 'that (thing) by which'; the translation 'nothing ... by which' is a loose rendering of 'that is not on earth nor in heaven by which the plants live'. brahma n.: sacred utterance; it could also be 'the great Brahmā/priest' (masc. would be brahmā). vīrudh = plants, creepers (general word).",
